            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "include/watchdog_event_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "Using quotes here is inconsistent with other files."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/watchdog_event_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Lei YU",
                        "email": "mine260309@gmail.com",
                        "username": "mine260309"
                    },
                    "message": "This is local hpp file, prefer to use \"\"\n\nBut this is likely OK to keep as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/watchdog_event_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "I meant that if you look in `include/threshold_event_monitor.hpp`, it still uses angle-braces.  If \"\" is preferred, that's fine, but we should use them consistently throughout all files in the repo."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/watchdog_event_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Lei YU",
                        "email": "mine260309@gmail.com",
                        "username": "mine260309"
                    },
                    "message": "OK, change it back."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/watchdog_event_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a reason that this is required?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/watchdog_event_monitor.hpp",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Lei YU",
                        "email": "mine260309@gmail.com",
                        "username": "mine260309"
                    },
                    "message": "It is to assign a \"default\" value so that the below `if (*expireAction == \"HardReset\")` can be retained.\nOtherwise, below `if/else if` will be changed to `if (expireAction && *expireAction == \"xxx\")`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 363,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "My only concern here is that the implementation of the various add functions is in two different files.  Why can the implementation be kept in the .cpp file?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 363,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Lei YU",
                        "email": "mine260309@gmail.com",
                        "username": "mine260309"
                    },
                    "message": "In c++, the template functions should be placed in hpp files because template instantiation requires full definition.\n\nclang-tidy complains:\n\n> error: function 'selAddSystemRecord<const char (&)[22], const char *, const char (&)[24], const char *, long>' has internal linkage but is not defined [clang-diagnostic-undefined-internal]"
                }
            ],
